ord-257bm-i11b"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i11b"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i11b","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 6.101 (Gap domination of the integer weights)","locator":"Long record Proposition 6.101, p. 73, label record:257bm-i11b","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For integers $1\\le d\\le R\\le M$, the quotient weights satisfy\n$$\n\\left\\lfloor\\frac{2^M}{2^d-1}\\right\\rfloor\n \\ge 2^{M-R}+\n \\sum_{j=d+1}^{R}\\left\\lfloor\\frac{2^M}{2^j-1}\\right\\rfloor.\n$$\nThus the finite weight list at ranks $2,\\ldots,R$ satisfies the hypothesis of Theorem 6.100 with $g=2^{M-R}$. At $M=2R-1$ this gap is $2^{R-1}$, and at $M=2R$ it is $2^R$. The inequality is unconditional; it does not assert that the greedy remainder is smaller than the gap.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i11b","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i11b","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i11b%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.BooleanMobiusGreedyReduction.localMersenneWeightsFrom_gapDominates%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i11b%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.BooleanMobiusGreedyReduction.localMersenneWeightsFrom_gapDominates%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.BooleanMobiusGreedyReduction.localMersenneWeightsFrom_gapDominates"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i11b","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e